        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><strong><span style='color: #000000;'><span style='color: #ff0000;'>CANCELLED |</span><i> ADULT ADVANCED VOICE OVER ACTING<br /></i></span></strong><span style='color: #000000;'><b><span style='font-size: 12pt;'>with Educator Pamela Hammond</span><br /></b></span></span></h4> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #ff0000;'>Unfortunately, this event has been cancelled.</span></p> <p><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>The Intro To Voice Over Announcing/Acting is a PREREQUISITE for this class.</span></strong><br /><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>&nbsp;</span><br /><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Expand your knowledge of Voice Over Acting and gain further experience to be on your way to a voice over career.&nbsp;Many students take this class just for fun, to break into the v/o industry or&nbsp; just&nbsp; to set up podcasts or videocasts.&nbsp;This course is mostly hands on with some lecturing.&nbsp;In this course you will learn timing. Some commercials and animations are read at a fast pace. Students will read scripts within the allotted time as well as voicing &#8220;cold reads&#8221;.&nbsp;Script Editing-Voicing one script 3 different ways as clients &amp; talent banks require many takes to choose from.&nbsp;The largest v/o markets are based in Chicago, New York and Los Angeles. You will learn various USA pronunciations.&nbsp;</span><br /><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Students will voice E-Learning, Narration, Jingles (even if you can&#8217;t sing), High Energy delivery, and fast paced scripts as well as character spots.&nbsp;</span><br /><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>6-Three hour sessions.</span></p> <h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>CLASS INFORMATION&nbsp;<br /></strong></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Mondays at 6:15PM | $165.00 per person<br /></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'>November 10 &#8211; December 15, 2025</span></span></span></h4> <hr> <h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>ABOUT OUR EDUCATOR<br /></strong></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>In 1998 Pamela got her start in voice acting by chance, voicing a short commercial for Global TV. Since then, she has voiced Internationally for TV &amp; Radio Commercials, Animation&nbsp;&amp; Gaming, Jingles, Narration &amp; Documentaries, Corporate Presentations, E-Learning, Social Media Ads and On Hold Messaging. In addition to voice acting, she has also produced spots with a few co-writing credits.<br /></span></h4> <h4><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>REGISTER ONLINE OR AT THE BOX OFFICE:</strong><br /></span></span><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong>604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM<br /></strong><strong><br /></strong></span></h4> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
