    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Paco_09.jpeg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g701480"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/rhs-paco-ha/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Rehearsal Hall Sessions: Paco Ha Jazz Quartet - Sketches"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h4><strong><span style='color: #000000;'><i>SKETCHES<br /></i>Paco Ha Jazz Quartet<br /></span></strong></h4> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>ABOUT THE SHOW<br /></strong></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Join the <strong>Paco Ha Quartet</strong> for <em>Sketches</em>, an evening of original compositions that blend </span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>diverse musical influences into the jazz quartet format. Drawing inspiration from various </span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>genres, such as impressionism, folk, and ambient music, Paco Ha&#8217;s work creates a rich </span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>soundscape that delves into texture, emotion, and depth. Expect melody-driven, powerful </span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>pieces that are both thought-provoking and captivating.</span></p> <p class='ewa-rteLine'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>With a focus on musical exploration and innovation, the performance promises to be an </span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>immersive experience, highlighting the versatility and creativity of the group. Paco Ha leads </span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>the ensemble with his melodic sound and innovative approach. Supported by a talented </span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>band, the quartet&#8217;s live performance will offer an intimate experience, exploring varied </span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>sounds within the jazz idiom while paying homage to the masters who paved the way for </span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>this music.</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>ABOUT THE ARTIST<br />Paco Ha </strong>is a tenor saxophonist based in Vancouver, drawing influence from jazz icons Joe Henderson and Kenny Garrett. As both a bandleader and sideman in various genres such as jazz, RnB, and pop, he has performed at various venues across the Lower Mainland and was featured at the Jazz at the Bolt Festival in 2025. In addition to his own projects, Paco co-leads projects like PATH and the Alice Coltrane Project, a collaboration with his sibling, Ru Ha. Known for his melodic sound and innovative approach, Paco is an up-and-coming saxophonist in the Vancouver jazz scene.<strong><br /></strong></span></p> <div>&nbsp;</div> <div>&nbsp;</div> <hr> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>SINGLE TICKETS ON SALE!</strong><br /></span></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Adults &amp; Seniors: $25 | Students: $16</span></p> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong>BOX OFFICE: 604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM</strong></span></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
