  {
    "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/linocut-workshop/event_35280_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/linocut-workshop/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/paulina-herpel-aeOvJ24HnFE-unsplash-scaled.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g1389760"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/linocut-workshop/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Linocut Workshop with Jordanna George"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000; font-size: 18.6667px;'>LINOCUT WORKSHOP<br /> </span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>with Jordanna George</span></strong></p> <div><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Join us for a beginner’s linocut workshop inspired by the exhibition&nbsp;<em>Sharni Pootoogook: Creatures, Shadows, and Dreams&nbsp;</em>at the Art Gallery at Evergreen hosted by artist Jordanna George.&nbsp;</span></div> <div>&nbsp;</div> <div><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>The workshop will begin with a brief tour of the exhibition. Afterwards, artist Jordanna George will lead you through hands-on techniques to carve and make your own prints with linocut.&nbsp; Free to attend, registration required.&nbsp;</span></div> <div>&nbsp;</div> <div><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><b>ABOUT OUR EDUCATOR</b></span></div> <div><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Jordanna George is an artist of mixed T’Sou-ke and Ukrainian ancestry. Originally from Sooke, BC, they now live on the unceded territories of the xʷməθkʷəy̓əm (Musqueam), Sḵwx̱wú7mesh (Squamish), səlilwətaʔɬ (Tsleil-Waututh), and kʷikʷəƛ̓əm (Kwikwetlem) nations in Coquitlam, BC. They received a BFA from the University of Victoria in 2019, and have since been making comics and illustrations, exploring themes of identity, belonging, and hope, and pulling influence from Indigeneity, queerness, and science fiction. The rest of Jordanna’s artistic practice involves painting, printmaking, and weaving. They can be found at&nbsp;<span style='color: #008000;'><u><a style='color: #008000;' href='http://jordannageorge.com/'>jordannageorge.com</a></u>&nbsp;</span>and on social media as @raebirdart.&nbsp;</span></div> <div>&nbsp;</div> <p><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>ABOUT THE EXHIBITION&nbsp;<br /> </span></span></strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><span class='TextRun SCXW228243050 BCX0' lang='EN-CA' xml:lang='EN-CA' data-contrast='auto'><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW228243050 BCX0'>Sharni Pootoogook (1922–2003) was a foundational yet under-recognized Inuit artist who used bold linework and balanced design to blur boundaries between human and animal, spiritual and physical, along the way shaping the trajectory of Inuit printmaking during a time of profound cultural change.</span></span><span class='EOP SCXW228243050 BCX0' data-ccp-props='{}'>&nbsp;</span></span></p> "
      }
    ],
