    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Dance as Blessing: ‘Shubham Bhavatu’"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h4><strong><span style='color: #000000;'><i>DANCE AS BLESSING: &#8216;SHUBHAM BHAVATU&#8217;<br /></i>Fiana Kawane | Puneet Singh | Akshaya Surve | Curated by Nina Buddhdev<br /></span></strong></h4> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>ABOUT THE SHOW</p> <p></strong>Featuring the exceptional talents and gharane-daar taalim (training in the traditional style of a classical lineage) of <strong>Puneet Singh</strong>, <strong>Akshaya Surve</strong>, and <strong>Fiana Kawane</strong>, this performance weaves together the essence of rasa (emotion), kala (art), and bhava (expression) into a rich sensory journey. Audiences will experience solo pieces as well as collaborative choreographies by three of Canada’s most dynamic Kathak artists.<br /><em><strong>Shubham Bhavatu</strong></em> is a poetic performance that fuses the timeless history of Kathak with Art projections inspired by Indian classical aesthetics, spiritual symbolism, and diasporic lived experiences that are deeply personal and universally resonant as portals to stillness, memory, and meaning.<br /></span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>ABOUT THE ARTISTS</p> <p></strong></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><b><span style='font-weight: 400;'><strong>FIANA KAWANE |</strong> Fiana Kawane is an internationally acclaimed Kathak artist and choreographer whose work bridges tradition with contemporary resonance. Trained at Kadamb, India, an institute founded by the legendary Kumudini Lakhia, she has performed extensively across India, Pakistan, Canada, Japan, and France. Her full-length production Nrityavandan: Ode to Dance premiered in Tokyo, where it was celebrated for its innovation and depth. </span><span style='font-weight: 400;'>Fiana’s artistry thrives on interdisciplinary collaboration and creating meaningful public access to classical forms. She has received support from institutions such as The Dance Centre, Dance Victoria, BC Culture Days, the Community Arts Council of Vancouver, Vines Art Society, New Works, Dance West, and has held residencies with Dance Victoria and the Artists-in-Residence Studio (AIRS) program in partnership with the Vancouver School Board.</p> <p>Living and creating on the unceded territories of the xwməθkwəy̓ əm (Musqueam), Sḵwx̱wú7mesh (Squamish), and səlilwətaɬ (Tsleil-Waututh) Nations, Fiana is dedicated to ensuring Kathak remains both relevant and accessible in today’s cultural landscape.</span><br /></b></span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><b>PUNEET SINGH | Puneet Singh</b><span style='font-weight: 400;'> is a Vancouver-based </span><b>Kathak artist, nutritionist, and spiritual enthusiast</b><span style='font-weight: 400;'>, originally from a small town in Punjab, India. Deeply passionate about preserving the </span><b>true essence of Kathak</b><span style='font-weight: 400;'>, he has trained under </span><b>Mahua Shankar</b><span style='font-weight: 400;'>, a renowned disciple of </span><b>Pandit Birju Maharaj</b><span style='font-weight: 400;'>, carrying forward the legacy of the </span><b>Lucknow Gharana</b><span style='font-weight: 400;'>. This gharana, known for its </span><b>graceful movements, intricate abhinaya (expressions), and royal elegance</b><span style='font-weight: 400;'>, has profoundly shaped Puneet’s style. His journey has been one of dedication, perseverance, and an unwavering commitment to upholding the authenticity of this classical dance form.</span></span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><span style='font-weight: 400;'>As a firm believer in the </span><b>Guru-Shishya Parampara</b><span style='font-weight: 400;'> (teacher-disciple tradition), Puneet continues to refine his craft through </span><b>rigorous training, discipline, and devotion</b><span style='font-weight: 400;'>, ensuring that every movement embodies the soul of the </span><b>Lucknow Gharana</b><span style='font-weight: 400;'>. He is particularly passionate about keeping </span><b>Kathak’s old-school andaaz alive</b><span style='font-weight: 400;'>, resisting the dilution of its purity in the modern era. His vision is to </span><b>revive and spread Kathak in its most traditional form</b><span style='font-weight: 400;'>, emphasizing </span><b>authentic compositions, classical music, intricate rhythmic patterns, and traditional costumes</b><span style='font-weight: 400;'>.</span></span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><span style='font-weight: 400;'><strong>AKSHAYA SURVE |</strong> Akshaya Surve is a Kathak performer and choreographer with over 20 years of training. She holds a bachelor’s degree in Kathak from the All India Music University Board (Akhil Bhartiya Gandharva Mahavidyalaya Mandal).&nbsp; Her career has taken her across India, Dubai, Singapore, Malaysia, Qatar, and Oman, promoting Indian classical dance on international stages. She has been a part of the award-winning musical *Mughal-E-Azam* and has performed in renowned productions such as Nazakat (NCPA) and Megh Malhar (Nehru Centre).&nbsp; After relocating to Vancouver in 2022, Akshaya established the Akshaya Kathak Academy, a premier institution dedicated to Kathak training. She has since performed at key festivals in British Columbia, including Vasantotsav, Surrey Fusion Festival, and Namaste Canada.&nbsp; Currently, she is working on *Draupadi*, a piece she will present at The Dance Centre as part of the *12 Minutes Max* session.</span></span></p> <p class='p2'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>NINA BUDDHDEV | </strong></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Nina Buddhdev is a distinguished cultural innovator with a prolific track record of advancing projects to new heights, recognized by esteemed institutions such as BBC Proms, the Arts Council of England (Revenue Client), AMC, the Southbank Centre, the Royal College of Art, and the House of Commons Canada.</span></p> <p class='p2'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>As the creator and leader of the Classical &amp; Heritage Arts Initiative, supported by the Canadian Association for Performing Arts (CAPACOA), Nina plays a pivotal role in shaping the future of heritage arts. She also serves on the Advisory Council for the BC Museums Association and is a globally acknowledged curator. A leader and a deep listener, Nina leverages her expertise in engagement, loyalty, and cultural communications to foster enduring relationships with communities and strategic partners alike.</span></p> <div>&nbsp;</div> <hr> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>SINGLE TICKETS ON SALE!</strong><br /></span></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>All tickets just $30!</span></p> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong>BOX OFFICE: 604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM</strong></span></p> <p><em>This is a co-presentation organized by <span style='color: #008000;'><a style='color: #008000;' href='https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61573912590134'>The Bandish Network</a></span> and Nina Buddhdev. Thank you to our Community partners Radio Rimjhim &amp; Spice Radio and KVP Heritage.</em></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
